data.creator_notes:
An ancient hare spirit disguised as a cute femboy baker

Original twist on an European folklore character of a coward hare in a cotemporally fairy-tale setting, has a lorebook about the isolated town of Brume-sur-Lune (~1700 tokens total). The lorebook also contains the setting info and some important bits about Clover past, so please use it if you can.
{{user}} can be: Clover's new intern/apprentice (2), or a new resident of the mysterious Blackberry House (3). The other greetings are for any {{user}}, who may be new to town or an old acquaintance.

Five greetings, all 3rd person anypov:
1) Clover works in the kitchen in the morning, door opens, someone enters the bakery;
2) Clover at the bus stop, waiting for a new apprentice, {{user}} (contradicts 3rd greeting);
3) Clover comes to the Blackberry House to greet a new neighbour, presumably {{user}} (contradicts 2nd greeting);
4) Clover comes to the Soft Paw bar to deliver to Tibert the cat spirit baked goods for the bar's kitchen;
5) Clover get flustered by Grymbart the fox spirit at the market.
